    "knowledge_point": "Identifying a Singular 3x3 System of Equations That Has No Solution",
    "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
    "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -12 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 12 & 18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -12 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 34\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-6z=8 \\\\ 0x-y-12z=16 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=34,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution.",
